  "query_preview": "..The sky was clear this morning under westerly\nflow aloft with water vapor imagery showing an upper love over\ncentral Utah. This low will move NE into Wyoming this afternoon.\nHighs today will be warmer than yesterday but still running\n5 to 10 degrees below normal for late May. May closes out\ntomorrow will normal or near normal highs with temperatures\n4 to 7 degrees warmer than today. Typical diurnal winds with \nafternoon gustiness due to heating.\n\nJune starts off with highs Monday at or a few degrees warmer \nthan Sunday with triple-digit highs returning to the lower\ndeserts of SE AZ. Highs will remain at or a few degrees above\nthru the end of next week. Moisture seep into the eastern areas\nnext week will bring a chance of afternoon and evening showers \nand thunderstorms mainly east of Tucson Tuesday thru Friday.\n\n8-14 day outlooks (June 6-12)\nTemperature: Likely above normal.\nPrecipitation: Leaning above normal most of the area.",
